  "caption": "Quinn did a 40-minute warm-up for a five-minute jog, was sore the next day anyway, and declared stretching a scam. A tiny bit dramatic.\n\nStretching doesn't do much to prevent soreness or injury. Strength training and sensible load changes tend to do more. Stretching can still improve range, and it often just feels nice.\n\nSome tips: put strength first, as full-range strength work can build flexibility too; use dynamic movement before sport; stretch the positions your life or sport needs, holding 30 to 60 seconds most days; and for desk stiffness, move more often.\n\nTingling when you stretch, sudden one-sided tightness, or pain that won't settle is worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
